==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*srew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|catarre}}, from {{der|en|ML.|catarrus}}, from {{der|en|LL.|catarrhus}}, from {{der|en|grc|κατάρροος}}, which is derived from {{m|grc|καταρρέω||I flow down}}, which is composed of {{m|grc|κατά||down}} and {{m|grc|ῥέω||I flow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈtɑɹ/}}
* {{homophones|en|Qatar}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} [[inflammation|Inflammation]] of the [[mucous membrane]]s of the [[nose]] and [[throat]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1851
|author=w:Herman Melville
|title=w:Moby Dick
|section=Chapter 3
|passage=Jonah mixed him a pitch-like potion of gin and molasses, which he swore was a sovereign cure for all colds and '''catarrhs''' whatsoever ...}}
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XII|passage=“Where I went wrong,” he said, still speaking in that low, husky voice as if he had been a ghost suffering from '''catarrh''', “was in getting engaged to Phyllis Mills.”}}
# A [[discharge]] of [[fluid]] associated with this condition. <!--e.g. one can "spit out catarrh"-->

